  "description": "Zero-copy interop between NumSharp NDArray and System.Numerics.Tensors (Tensor<T>, TensorSpan<T>, ReadOnlyTensorSpan<T>). View an NDArray of any layout — contiguous, sliced, transposed, strided or broadcast — as a TensorSpan<T> over the very same unmanaged buffer (no copy), read a Tensor<T> back as an NDArray (copy or zero-copy view), and hand tensors to the BCL's SIMD TensorPrimitives without a fill loop. Conversion library only: no engine backend, no ModuleInitializer, no native dependency. All 15 NumSharp dtypes cross as their own CLR type (Half, Complex, Decimal, char included).",
